message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "llmsa: Measurement System Analysis for Pipelines Built on Large Language Models"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-20
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DanielMoj/llmsa"
url: "https://github.com/DanielMoj/llmsa"
authors:
  - family-names: Moj
    given-names: Daniel Andreas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-1594-6065"
keywords:
  - measurement system analysis
  - gauge R&R
  - large language models
  - validation
  - variance components
  - robustness
  - Plackett-Burman
  - Westgard rules
  - R package
abstract: >-
  Treats a pipeline built on a large language model as a measurement system
  and validates it with crossed precision studies (variance components,
  gauge repeatability and reproducibility), attribute agreement (Krippendorff's
  alpha, Cohen's kappa), bias and linearity, Plackett-Burman robustness
  screening with Lenth's method, simulation-based study planning,
  Westgard-rule control charts and a reproducible validation report.
